Chapter 18: The Strategist Unwinds

[Haven Chat Log - Day 262, 9:45 PM]

Lina: dr vance, you've been quiet tonight.

Dr_A_Vance: I have been thinking about childhood. A strange topic for a man my age.

Jon: Not strange at all. Childhood is where everything starts.

Dr_A_Vance: Lina's story about the protein folding lecture reminded me. Nature doesn't waste mistakes. I have been wondering if that applies to me.

Lina: of course it applies to you. you're nature too.

Dr_A_Vance: When I was a boy, I was afraid of my father's study. It was a dark room with heavy furniture and the smell of old paper. He was a professor. Handa, in fact. Before my time here.

Jon: You're second-generation Handa.

Dr_A_Vance: Third. My grandfather taught here as well. The study was originally his.

Lina: a legacy of dark rooms.

Dr_A_Vance: Yes. I would stand at the door and feel a terror I could not name. It was not my father. He was a kind man. It was something about the room itself. The weight of expectation. The sense that serious things happened there, and I was not yet serious enough to enter.

eli: did you ever go in?

Dr_A_Vance: Eventually. I had to. My father wanted to show me a book. An old illustrated astronomy text. I remember thinking the stars looked like punctuation marks.

Jon: That's a beautiful image.

Dr_A_Vance: The fear didn't disappear. But it shared space with something else. Curiosity. The room was still dark, but it was also full of stars.

Lina: you just described healing, dr vance. the fear doesn't go away. it just makes room for other things.

Dr_A_Vance: I have never told anyone that story. I am not sure why I am telling it now.

eli: because it's 10 PM and we're strangers on a screen. sometimes that's easier.

Dr_A_Vance: Perhaps. Or perhaps because I trust you.

Jon: We trust you too.

Dr_A_Vance: I should delete that message. It was unprofessional. I seemed to have forgotten for a moment that this was not a private journal.

Jon: Or maybe you remembered it's not just a public chat either, Dr. Vance.

Dr_A_Vance: Yes. Perhaps that is it.

