Mira: i know it was bad. i was there.

Sid: [Admin] then you know they're not going to let this go. they want full integration by next semester or they're pulling server access.

Mira: i know, sid. i was in the room.

Sid: [Admin] so what's the plan? we can't just wait.

Mira: maybe there isn't a plan. maybe this was always going to happen.

Sid: [Admin] that's not the mira who built this at 2 AM.

Mira: the mira who built this at 2 AM was naive. she thought a good thing could just exist.

Sid: [Admin] it did exist. it does exist. there are people in the chat right now.

Mira: and what happens when handa shuts it down? what do i tell them? sorry, i tried, but the institution won?

Sid: [Admin] you tell them the truth.

Mira: the truth is i'm exhausted. the truth is i can't fight a university by myself.

Sid: [Admin] you're not by yourself.

Mira: you've been practical from the start. you said this might happen. you were right.

Sid: [Admin] i didn't want to be right. i wanted to be wrong.

Mira: maybe we should just let them absorb it. let it become another official handa platform with moderation and policies and no soul.

[System Message: Content deleted.]

Sid: [Admin] mira.

[System Message: Content deleted.]

Mira: i can't. i can't do this tonight.

[System Message: Mira has left the room.]

[Public Chat - Same Time]

eli: did anyone else just see that?

Lina: see what?

eli: the admin channel glitched. two messages showed up in public for like three seconds.

Jon: What did they say?

eli: "should just let them absorb it, what else can we" and "never meant to be forever, Mira, you knew the"

Lina: oh no.

Jon: They're fighting.

Lina: they're not fighting. they're scared. there's a difference.

eli: scared looks like fighting when you're in charge.

Lina: what do we do?

Jon: We keep being here. That's all we can do.

eli: that's not enough.

Jon: It's what we have.

