Chapter 23: The Defeated Defender

[Haven Chat Log - Day 338, 8:00 PM]

Dr_A_Vance: I presented the data today.

Lina: dr vance!! what data?

Dr_A_Vance: The engagement metrics. The crisis intervention on Day 245. The consistent mental health support this community provides. The testimony from users who said Haven helped them feel less isolated during exams, during personal difficulties, during the quiet hours when the rest of campus feels closed.

Jon: What did they say?

Dr_A_Vance: They thanked me for my thoroughness.

eli: that's not a yes.

Dr_A_Vance: No. It is not.

Lina: what does that mean?

Dr_A_Vance: It means the decision was made before I walked into the room. The data was an inconvenience. The testimony was an anecdote. Policy 14.7 is moving forward regardless.

Jon: You did everything you could.

Dr_A_Vance: I presented the data. The connection. The case of the storm. The night we stayed with Guest_139. I told them about the typo. "tomoroww." I told them about the hum of the heating system and how this space makes people feel like they exist.

Lina: you told them all of that?

Dr_A_Vance: I am not a strategist here. I am just an old man who is very, very sad.

Jon: Dr. Vance.

Dr_A_Vance: I am sorry. I failed. I am not sure they ever intended to listen.

eli: you didn't fail. you fought.

Dr_A_Vance: I fought with spreadsheets and policy arguments. It was not enough.

Lina: it was more than anyone else on the inside did.

Dr_A_Vance: I wanted to save this place. Not for the institution. For myself. For all of you.

Jon: You're part of this community, Dr. Vance. You always have been.

Dr_A_Vance: I am realizing that now. Too late.

eli: it's not too late. we're still here.

Dr_A_Vance: For how much longer?

[Timestamp: 8:15 PM]

Jon: For as long as the cursor blinks.

---

Chapter 24: The Self-Policing

[Haven Chat Log - Day 352, 11:30 PM]

Guest_204: HEY IS ANYONE HERE?? THIS PLACE IS SO QUIET WHAT THE HELL

Lina: shh. please don't shout.

Guest_204: what? why?

Lina: we have to be quiet or they'll take it away.

Guest_204: who's "they"?

eli: the administration. they're monitoring. caps lock makes us look bad.

Guest_204: that's the dumbest thing i've ever heard. it's a chat room.

Jon: It's not just a chat room. It's a space that's under review. We need to be careful.

Guest_204: careful about what? having fun?

Lina: careful about giving them reasons.

Guest_204: reasons for what? i just got here. someone said this was a cool place to hang out.

eli: it was. it is. just keep it down.

Guest_204: whatever. this is weird.

[System Message: Guest_204 has left the room.]

Jon: Eli... listen to yourself.

eli: what.

Jon: "Caps lock makes us look bad." We're policing how people type. This is what they wanted.

eli: i know.

Jon: A panopticon where we do the work for them. Where we're so afraid of losing the space that we destroy what made it a space in the first place.

eli: i know. i know. i just don't know what else to do.

Lina: we just scared off a new user. someone who heard this was a cool place and came to find out why.

eli: and we told them to be quiet.

Jon: We told them to be afraid.

Lina: when did we become the thing we were afraid of?

eli: when we got something to lose.

Jon: So we lose it by protecting it.

eli: that's the trap. that's the whole trap.

Lina: then we stop. right now. we stop policing. we stop being careful. we be what we were.

Jon: What were we?

Lina: loud. weird. full of kaomojis. honest.

eli: i don't know if i remember how.

Lina: then we learn again. starting now.

